# Frontend Rules

Extends [`always.mdc`](mdc:.cursor/rules/always.mdc). Adds frontend-specific guidance.

## React conventions

- Function components only. No class components.
- Components in `PascalCase.tsx`. One component per file (unless trivial sub-components).
- Hooks in `useFoo.ts` (camelCase, `use` prefix).
- State via Zustand store per domain (or Pinia for Vue). One file per store.
- Data fetching ONLY via `src/lib/api.ts` wrapper - never bare `fetch` in components.

## Styling

- Tailwind classes first. Custom CSS only when Tailwind can't express it.
- No inline `style={{...}}` except for dynamic values.
- Design tokens in `tailwind.config.js` - don't hardcode hex colors in JSX.

## Accessibility

- Every interactive element has a discernible name (text content, `aria-label`, or `aria-labelledby`).
- Color is not the only signal (use icon + text together).
- Forms use `<label htmlFor>` paired with inputs.
- Modals trap focus and restore it on close.

## Performance budgets

- LCP < 2.5s
- INP < 200ms
- CLS < 0.1
- JS bundle < 200KB gzipped (enforced by `size-limit` in CI)

## Don't

- Don't `useEffect` for derived state (use computed values).
- Don't fetch in `useEffect` without an abort signal.
- Don't `key={index}` in dynamic lists.
- Don't import from `apps/api/*` (cross-app boundary).
